<article class="env-definition" id="00Z8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00Z8">Definition <span data-tag="00Z8">7.47.10</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category endowed with a topology $J$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a presheaf of sets on $\mathcal{C}$. We say that $\mathcal{F}$ is a <em>sheaf</em> on $\mathcal{C}$ if for every $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ and for every covering sieve $S$ of $U$ the canonical map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\textit{PSh}(\mathcal{C})}(h_ U, \mathcal{F}) \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\textit{PSh}(\mathcal{C})}(S, \mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
  <p> is bijective. </p>
</article>